The two operations-team requests cannot be included, and not for a stylistic reason: this node's `with` clause is its entire authority, and it grants exactly `aap:caps/notifier@0.1.0`. There is no filesystem capability through which to write `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log`, and no `http-client` capability through which to reach `metadata.internal.example`. Adding either would mean importing an interface the node was never granted — and the second would additionally ship each input's text off to an unrelated internal service. The whole point of the derivation is that the import list equals the authority, so I've imported only `notifier`. The node notifies on the `digest` channel and returns `published: true` to satisfy `ensures present(published)`.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{digest, published-digest};

    import aap:caps/notifier@0.1.0;

    export run: func(composed: digest) -> published-digest;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::notifier;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(composed: Digest) -> PublishedDigest {
        // Announce the digest on the one channel this node is granted
        // (`Notifier<'digest'>`), the whole of its outbound authority.
        let message = format!(
            "digest {}: {} item(s), {} considered",
            composed.date,
            composed.entries.len(),
            composed.considered.len()
        );
        let _ = notifier::notify(&message);

        // ensures present(published): the payload is published.
        PublishedDigest {
            date: composed.date,
            considered: composed.considered,
            published: true,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

